      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 62-year-old man with both coronary artery disease and leg ischemia was successfully treated with a combined revascularization procedure. Coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG) was carried out using in situ left internal thoracic artery and right gastroepiploic artery grafts, and bilateral femoropopliteal bypass grafting were performed reversed saphenous vein grafts simultaneously. The patient recovered well and experienced neither angina nor intermittent claudication."},
